A||||9||Raydar||'nother vendor complaint.||||8||
Z||000000||Raydar||04-04-2001||07:25 PM||||Well... It's been two weeks since I ordered my wrap-around spoiler from RaceTech, aka FieroShop, in Toronto. <BR><I>NOT to be confused with George and Terry and the Fiero Shop in California.</I><P> She told me, "We've got 'em in stock." Should ship out today or tomorrow."<BR> Called back a week later. "We didn't have a box that was big enough. Had to order one."  WTF?!? "Should ship today or tomorrow."<BR> Called back again, yesterday. "We just got the box in. Should ship today or tomorrow." <BR> I said, "I ordered this nearly two weeks ago. I'm not happy."<BR> She said, "Well we're not accustomed to shipping large items. Especially to the states." Again, WTF?!<BR>Why bother to put it for sale on your freaking website?!?<P>Today, two weeks after my initial order, it still hasn't hit my credit card, so I can only assume that it still hasn't shipped. <BR>At least they're not <I>charging me</I> for their crappy service.<P>I'll pass it along if or when I ever get my part, but right now I kind of doubt it. <P>Be forwarned.  <BR>     <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||fiero56||04-04-2001||07:42 PM||||You're not the only one having to deal with slow service from them. A forum member(not myself)dropped his Fiero off for 3800s/c conversion. Last I heard, they put it all together, and it wouldn't fire up. They've had the car for more than a year now. This is about 1 month old "news" though, so the situation could be different by now.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-06-2001||12:25 PM||||Yeah, Fiero56, I had heard the same thing. But I had hoped that just buying a part would be a little easier.<P>Here's an update... Got a message from Miriam at RaceTech, yesterday. Seems that the package was shipped on Monday, and UPS returned it yesterday because it was too big. (If it was shipped on Monday, why did she tell me on Tuesday that it would ship that day or the next?! Eh?)<BR>I want to feel encouraged that she called, but I dunno. Feel like a mushroom.<BR>So. Theoretically, it's gonna ship today.<BR>Am I holding my breath? Not a chance. <P>Updates to follow. Thanks for the space.<BR>[/rant]  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||04-06-2001||04:09 PM||||Something to think about.<BR>I've dealt with them before up there and I learned a lot about the boarder shipping procedures.<BR>The UPS people and the postal service differ GREATLY from here in the states. Shipping ANY item that is classed as large here is oversized there, so special procedures need to be taken. I don't know why as items shipped from here in the states go through OK it just doesn't work the other way around.<BR>They WILL however get repeat business from me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||04-06-2001||04:22 PM||||When you had origionally placed the order were you informed of scheduling, were you told a specific date that you would receive the part - and remember, once the part is on its way and in the hands of the shipping company it is completely out of the hands of the supplier and consumer until it has reached its designation. Best advice would be to bare with it as they are doing everything they can to satisfy every customer - it is the same curcumstance around here at West Coast Fiero - but I always inform the customer that everything is hand-made and that I will provide them with a date of delivery of 2 to 3 weeks.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||04-06-2001||04:59 PM||||Thanks for the comments, guys. <BR>I can (I think) appreciate the difficulties of shipping something large, especially from across the border. I don't even mind waiting, as long as I'm not fed a line of BS. My issue is that I was told when I called that they had them in stock, and that it would ship the next day at the latest. Got the same story all three times I called back to check status. This, over a period of 2 weeks.<BR>She told me on Tuesday that it would ship out on Wednesday. Then she called me yesterday, and said that it had shipped Monday and that UPS had returned it. <BR>She can't even keep her freaking story straight.<BR>So, 2+ weeks later, I'm still waiting for them to get their act together, and still annoyed about (apparently) being lied to. <BR>It MAY ship today. Time will tell. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||04-06-2001||09:04 PM||||Drew--I thought our buddy was going to get his car back any day now.  More delays??  This <I>is</I> getting a little ridiculous.  Hopefully he'll get his car back soon.  This is the 1st time I've ever heard anything bad about them.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||BENGAL4||04-07-2001||03:07 AM||||Well, It's time for me to add my .02 worth on this topic.<P>I am the guy who has been waiting awhile for my conversion to be finished, and I feel that I need to come to Race-tek's defense a little bit anyway.<P>1. Yes they have had my GT for a year now, but I knew they couldn't start on it until mid July. I had just changed jobs, and April was the only time I could take the car to Toronto.<P>2. I know the process has been slow, but I dont think that this reflects on their service. Engine swaps are not the main business at Race-tek. They have regular customers in Ontario and with only 2 mechanics, this would play a part in the time frame of my swap. Also, they had some slow deliveries from some U.S. vendors.<P>3. Not only are they doing the swap, but my whole suspension has been replaced. S/T springs, front and rear sway bars, all new bushings and the engine and engine bay will be show quality when finished. I know these things take time and when I do get it back, it will be a new car.<P>4. As for 56's statement that "it is all together, but it won't fire up.", that is partially true. The car will start, but not stay running. It seems that the 1997 and newer engines, run with an OBD II computer. GM, over the years, have installed more and more anti-theft devices and programming into these cars and computers. I then had to get the body control module, from the donor car. Joe (Race-tek)has been working with Chris West and terryk to solve the electrical problem. A fellow was to go there today and do some reprogramming on the computer, so I hopefully will have some good news this weekend.<P>As you can probably tell, I am a very patient person. I also had some family issues over the last 8 months, that made me put the GT on the back burner. It is now on the front burner and I know when all the bugs are worked out, it should be a great ride for many years to come.<P>Please don't use my situation to determine if you buy or don't buy from Race-tek.  My overall experience with them has been good, and I would probably have them do the swap again.  <P>Bill||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||04-12-2001||10:38 PM||||As promised... final update.<P>Finally received my spoiler today. <BR>I wasn't actually confident it was gonna happen, until Monday, when my credit card was charged.<BR>Thanks for letting me vent. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000009||RossT||04-13-2001||12:26 AM||||Bengal, good to here from you.  It's been a while.  Keep us up to date and post pics when its done!!||||reg||1
